al pronouns).\n            \\item \\textbf{Thematic Features:} Topic distributions derived from Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) that describe \\textit{what} the text is about.\n        \\end{enumerate}\n        \n        This leads to our primary research questions:\n        \\begin{itemize}\n            \\item[\\textbf{Q1:}] To what extent can the fundamental differences between human and LLM texts be quantified through a measurable set of linguistic features?\n            \\item[\\textbf{Q2:}] Can the proposed multi-feature representation effectively  distinguish one LLM from another?\n        \\end{itemize}\n        \\vspace{1.5\\baselineskip}\n\n\\subsection{Novelty}\n        \\vspace{0.5\\baselineskip}\n        % [수정] 사용자가 요청한 원래의 도입 문장 구조를 사용\n        The novelty of this work is defined by two key contributions that, when combined, create our analytical framework:\n        \n        \\begin{itemize}\n            % [수정] 1번 기여: 교수님 키워드 \"combination\" 사용\n            \\item \\textbf{A Deliberate Combination of Heterogeneous Features:} \n            Our first contribution is the deliberate \\textbf{combination} of two fundamentally different feature categories. We constructed a hybrid vector that integrates (1) stylistic metrics, which describe \\textit{how} a text is written, with (2) thematic distributions, which represent \\textit{what} a text is about. This approach creates a single, richer feature set designed to capture a more holistic view of a text\u0027s origin than single-aspect methods allow.\n\n            % [수정] 2번 기여: 교수님 키워드 \"analytics of results obtained\" 개념 반영\n            \\item \\textbf{The Analysis of Obtained Feature Interactions:}\n            Our second contribution lies in the \\textbf{analysis of the results obtained} from this complex hybrid vector. We employ a Deep Neural Network (DNN) specifically to uncover the non-linear interactions between the combined stylistic and thematic features. Instead of treating features independently, the DNN analyzes how they relate to each other, providing a deeper, more contextual understanding. This analytical step is crucial for leveraging the full potential of the feature combination.\n        \\end{itemize}\n        \\vspace{1.5\\baselineskip}\n\t\t\\end{quote}\n    }\n}\n% --- 다음 페이지로 나눕니다 ---\n\\newpage\n\n% --- 요약문 2페이지 ---\n\\noindent\\fbox{\n    \\parbox{\\textwidth}{\n    \t\\begin{quote}      \n\t\t\\subsection{Algorithms}\n\t\t\\vspace{0.5\\baselineskip}\n        \n        % [수정] 사용자 요청대로, 도입 문장을 먼저 작성\n        Our methodology is implemented as a systematic pipeline, beginning with corpus construction followed by a three-step classification process.\n        \n        % [수정] 도입 문장 아래에 번호 목록이 시작되도록 구조 수정\n        \\begin{enumerate}\n            \\item \\textbf{Data Collection and Preprocessing:}\n            The foundation of our study is a carefully constructed corpus. The final dataset comprises a total of \\textbf{14,832 documents}, sourced from 5 distinct \\textbf{sources}: four LLMs and human \\textbf{sources}. For text from human \\textbf{sources}, we sourced data from Quora, ensuring all answers were posted at least five years prior to mitigate potential LLM contamination. We identified approximately \\textbf{100 unique questions} and sampled up to 30 answers per question. To generate the LLM-generated text, we used the same set of questions as prompts for four LLM \\textbf{sources} (Claude, DeepSeek, Gemini, GPT). The entire corpus then underwent a standardized preprocessing pipeline, including lowercasing, tokenization, and the removal of stopwords and special characters.\n\n             \\item \\textbf{Analytical Pipeline:}\n            Following data preparation, the preprocessed data was passed through the following three-step pipeline:\n            \n            \\begin{center}\n            \\vspace{0.5\\baselineskip}\n            % [수정] tabular를 버리고, 너비를 직접 제어하는 방식으로 변경하여 레이아웃 문제 완전 해결\n            \\noindent\\fbox{%\n                \\parbox{0.29\\textwidth}{\n                    \\centering\n                    \\textbf{Step 1: Feature Engineering}\n                    \\begin{itemize}\n                        \\setlength\\itemsep{0em}\n                        \\item Stylistic features were computed.\n                        \\item Thematic features were derived.\n                    \\end{itemize}\n                }%\n            }\\hfill%\n            $\\rightarrow$\\hfill%\n            \\fbox{%\n                \\parbox{0.29\\textwidth}{\n                    \\centering\n                    \\textbf{Step 2: Feature Concatenation}\n                    \\begin{itemize}\n                        \\setlength\\itemsep{0em}\n                        \\item Stylistic and thematic vectors were combined.\n                        \\item A single vector was created per document.\n                    \\end{itemize}\n                }%\n            }\\hfill%\n            $\\rightarrow$\\hfill%\n            \\fbox{%\n                \\parbox{0.29\\textwidth}{\n                    \\centering\n                    \\textbf{Step 3: DNN Classification}\n                    \\begin{itemize}\n                        \\setlength\\itemsep{0em}\n                        \\item The combined vector served as input.\n                        \\item A DNN model predicted the text source.\n                    \\end{itemize}\n                }%\n            }\n            \\vspace{0.5\\baselineskip}\n            \\end{center}\n        \\end{enumerate}\n\t\t\\vspace{1.5\\baselineskip}\n\n        % [수정 완료] 실제 DNN 결과와 연구 질문을 연결한 최종 버전\n        % [수정 완료] 실제 DNN 결과와 연구 질문을 연결한 최종 버전\n        % [수정 완료] Q2가 삭제됨에 따라, 해당 내용 제거 및 문장 수정\n\n        \\subsection{Experiments}\n\t\t\\vspace{0.5\\baselineskip}\n        \n        % [수정] 요청대로 세 가지 항목의 핵심 내용을 하나의 문단으로 통합 및 강조\n        To validate our framework, we conducted a classification experiment using a hold-out validation method. Our dataset of 14,832 documents was partitioned into training (80\\%) and test (20\\%) sets with a fixed random state to ensure reproducibility. The DNN model, trained on the comprehensive hybrid features, was rigorously evaluated on the unseen test set and achieved an \\textbf{overall accuracy of 82.2\\%}. As detailed in Figure 1 and 2, the model demonstrated strong performance, notably classifying human-sourced text with the highest accuracy (F1-Score: \\textbf{0.902}) and effectively differentiating among LLMs.\n        \n        % [수정] Analysis of Results는 나중에 추가할 수 있도록 일단 비워둠\n        \n        % [수정] 그림 배치 코드는 그대로 유지\n        \\begin{center}\n        \\noindent\\makebox[\\textwidth]{%\n            \\begin{minipage}{0.4\\textwidth}\n                \\centering\n                \\includegraphics[width\u003d0.85\\linewidth]{confusion_matrix.png} \n                \\textbf{Figure 1:} Confusion Matrix\n            \\end{minipage}%\n            \\hfill\n            \\begin{minipage}{0.6\\textwidth}\n                \\centering\n                \\includegraphics[width\u003d0.75\\linewidth]{classification_report.png} \n                \\\\[0.5\\baselineskip]\n                \\textbf{Figure 2:} Classification Report\n            \\end{minipage}%\n        }\n        \\end{center}\n\t\\end{quote}\n    }\n}\n% --- 마지막 요약 페이지의 페이지 번호가 보이지 않게 처리 ---\n\\thispagestyle{empty}\n\n\\end{document}\n\n자 여기서 이제 AI 논문에서 사용하지 않는 표현, 비문, 어려운표현(풀어쓸 수 있는) 찾아서 수정해 ",
