ote}      \n\t\t% [수정] Algorithm 섹션의 나머지 부분 (Analytical Pipeline)\n\t\t\\vspace{1.5\\baselineskip} % 윗 공간 확보\n        \\textbf{Analytical Pipeline:}\n        The preprocessed data was passed through the following three-step pipeline:\n        \\begin{center}\n        \\vspace{0.5\\baselineskip}\n        \\includegraphics[width\u003d1\\linewidth]{boxes.png} \n        \\end{center}\n        \\vspace{1.5\\baselineskip} % 섹션 간 간격 조정\n\n        \\subsection{Experiments}\n\t\t\\vspace{0.5\\baselineskip}\n        To validate our framework, we conducted a classification experiment using a hold-out validation method. Our dataset of 14,832 documents was partitioned into training (80\\%) and test (20\\%) sets with a fixed random state to ensure reproducibility. The DNN model, trained on the comprehensive hybrid features, was evaluated on the unseen test set and achieved an overall accuracy of 82.2\\%. \n        \n        The detailed results are presented in the figures below. As shown in the confusion matrix (Figure 1), the model successfully differentiated among the sources, identifying human-sourced text with the highest accuracy (F1-Score: \\textbf{0.902}). The boxplot of the Personal Pronoun (PRP) ratio (Figure 2) provides a clear explanation for this success: human texts exhibit a consistently higher PRP ratio, which serves as a powerful linguistic fingerprint.\n\n        Furthermore, a separate feature importance analysis confirmed the effectiveness of our hybrid approach. While a model trained only on thematic (LDA) features achieved a notable accuracy of 63.2\\%, the full combination of features yielded a significantly higher performance. This demonstrates that while LDA features form the primary basis for classification, the inclusion of stylistic features is crucial for capturing the more nuanced differences between sources and maximizing the model\u0027s overall efficacy.\n\n        \\begin{center}\n            \\includegraphics[width\u003d0.9\\linewidth]{combined_exp.png}\n        \\end{center\u003e\n        \n        While our framework is effective for distinct sources, future work should extend this approach to detect more complex, mixed-authorship texts (mixtexts), a growing challenge in the field (e.g., Zhang et al., 2024).\n\t\\end{quote}\n    }\n}\n% --- 마지막 요약 페이지의 페이지 번호가 보이지 않게 처리 ---\n\\thispagestyle{empty}\n\n\\end{document}\n```\n\n### **이번 수정의 핵심**\n\n1.  **`Problem Setup` 압축:**\n    *   기존의 여러 문장을 하나로 합치고, `enumerate`와 `itemize` 목록을 줄글로 풀어 설명하여 공간을 크게 줄였습니다.\n2.  **`Novelty` 압축:**\n    *   두 가지 기여를 설명하는 내용을 각각 한 문장으로 압축하여 핵심만 전달하도록 했습니다.\n3.  **`Algorithm` 섹션 분리:**\n    *   `Algorithm` 섹션을 시작하면서, 그 안의 `Data Collection and Preprocessing:` 파트를 1페이지의 남은 공간에 배치했습니다.\n    *   `Analytical Pipeline:` 파트는 2페이지의 시작 부분으로 자연스럽게 넘어갑니다.\n\n이렇게 수정함으로써, 요청하신 대로 **`Data Collection and Preprocessing` 내용까지 모두 1페이지에 포함**되도록 했습니다. 다만, 보시다시피 1페이지의 내용이 매우 압축적이 되었으므로, 최종 제출 전에 내용이 충분히 전달되는지 다시 한번 확인해 보시는 것을 추천합니다.",
